  "question": {
    "text": "Let $A(-3,2)$ and $B(-2,1)$ be the vertices of a triangle $\\mathrm{ABC}$. If the centroid of this triangle lies on the line $3 x+4 y+2=0$, then the vertex $C$ lies on the line :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "Urf6a",
      "text": "\n$4 x+3 y+5=0$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "tEZ7v",
      "text": "\n $3 x+4 y+3=0$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JYoeU",
      "text": "\n$4 x+3 y+3=0$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "pljrL",
      "text": "\n$3 x+4 y+5=0$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let $\\mathrm{C}=\\left(x_1, y_1\\right)$\n$$\n\\mathrm{A}(-3,2)\n$$\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/qEa6UjFUKrQAArbX4sA8PR4lHPLLAsDoNjZyb6BUsQA.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\nCentroid, $\\mathrm{E}=\\left(\\frac{x_1-5}{3}, \\frac{y_1+3}{3}\\right)$\nSince centroid lies on the line\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& 3 x+4 y+2=0 \\\\\n\\therefore \\quad & 3\\left(\\frac{x_1-5}{3}\\right)+4\\left(\\frac{y_1+3}{3}\\right)+2=0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n$$\n\\Rightarrow \\quad 3 x_1+4 y_1+3=0\n$$\nHence vertex $\\left(x_1, y_1\\right)$ lies on the line\n$$\n3 x+4 y+3=0\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
